-- title:
--   Proj of a coefficient homomorphism restricts to the Z-chart
-- statement:
--   Let $T$ and $T'$ be commutative rings in a fixed universe, $W$ a projective Weierstrass curve over $T$ and $f : T \to T'$ a ring homomorphism, so that $W.map f$ is the projective Weierstrass curve over $T'$ obtained by applying $f$ to the coefficients. Write $\mathcal{A}(V)$ for the quotient $T[X_0,X_1,X_2]/(F_V)$ of the polynomial ring in three variables by the ideal generated by the Weierstrass cubic of $V$, graded by `projModelGradingCR V`, the images of the homogeneous submodules under the quotient map. Let $\varphi : \mathcal{A}(W) \to \mathcal{A}(W.map f)$ be a homomorphism of graded rings such that the irrelevant ideal of $\mathcal{A}(W.map f)$ is contained in the image under $\varphi$ of the irrelevant ideal of $\mathcal{A}(W)$, and assume `IsCoefficientHom W f φ`, i.e. $\varphi$ carries the class of a constant $C a$ to the class of $C (f a)$ for all $a \in T$, and fixes the class of each variable $X_i$, $i \in \mathrm{Fin}\ 3$. Then there is a ring homomorphism $a$ from $\mathrm{ZChartRing}\,W$, the degree-zero part of the localisation of $\mathcal{A}(W)$ away from the class $Z$ of $X_2$, to $\mathrm{ZChartRing}\,(W.map f)$, such that the chart inclusion $\mathrm{zChart}\iota$ for $W.map f$ followed by $\mathrm{Proj.map}\ \varphi$ equals $\mathrm{Spec}(a)$ followed by the chart inclusion $\mathrm{zChart}\iota$ for $W$, and such that $a$ sends $X/Z$ to $X/Z$ and $Y/Z$ to $Y/Z$ (the elements `xOverZ`, `yOverZ` given by the degree-zero fractions with numerators the classes of $X_0$, $X_1$ and denominator $Z$). The proof uses only the second clause of `IsCoefficientHom`, the one asserting that $\varphi$ fixes the classes of the three variables.
--
--   This is the compatibility of $\mathrm{Proj}$ functoriality with the standard affine chart $D_+(Z)$: a graded homomorphism induced by base change along $f$ restricts on the finite chart to $\mathrm{Spec}$ of a map of chart rings which preserves the affine coordinates $X/Z$ and $Y/Z$. It is the base-change mechanism used downstream when points of Weierstrass models are compared in affine coordinates on one chart, for instance in the Frobenius-type statement [`WeierstrassCurve.DrinfeldGlobal.comp_projMap_eq_frobenius_of_zChart_pow_originChart_pow`](thm.html#WeierstrassCurve.DrinfeldGlobal.comp_projMap_eq_frobenius_of_zChart_pow_originChart_pow) and in the level-structure constructions that cite it.
